{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>A time to cast.</b> Even an incidental occurrence has its time, like a time to cast stones — when they trouble him in his dwelling — a time to gather them, the cast ones, for his needs." "<b>A time to embrace.</b> Even the desire implanted in the spirit of man has a time: to embrace her who lies in the bosom, and to keep away from her." "<b>To embrace.</b> From the light binyan (קל)." "<b>And to embrace.</b> From the heavy binyan with a dagesh, and the meaning is the same."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:14.249408699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}